    <note id="blA">
      <content>
        <p>We want to be candid about what the system is and is not. It outputs probabilities, not certainties, and a genuinely unprecedented event cannot be forecast; we show the bands and keep the tails open. The quality of a prediction depends on the quality of the world spec, which is why specs are typed and the simulator is deterministic. Calibration is only as good as the case library, and we are growing it while disclosing how close the nearest case is. On edge cases, generation can still fail, so gates and a template fallback protect the output and a human reviews. The system is a decision aid that makes trade-offs visible, not a replacement for judgment. We believe this honesty is itself a reason to trust the numbers.</p>
      </content>
    </note>
